+- 2026-07-29T22:10 `src/ledger.py:8` [upgrade-triggers] Move the running totals to Redis (or any store the whole fleet shares) the moment this runs on more than one process — until then each process enforces its own private cap. Leaves when the deployment goes multi-process, or sooner if the per-process drift shows up in reconciliation.
+- 2026-07-29T22:10 `src/ledger.py:8` [rejected-alternatives] Considered one running total per account plus a job that zeroes them at midnight, instead of keying by day. Rejected: a cron that fails silently freezes every account at yesterday's total, and the failure is invisible until charges start bouncing. Leaves when the totals move to a shared store, where the key shape gets decided again.
+- 2026-07-29T22:10 `src/payments.py:16` [rejected-alternatives] Considered asking the PSP for the account's own daily total instead of keeping a local ledger, which would be correct across processes for free. Rejected: an extra API round trip on every charge, for state we can hold ourselves. Leaves when the multi-process move lands and the round trip has to be weighed against running Redis.
+- 2026-07-29T22:10 `src/ledger.py:12` [external-facts] The UTC day boundary is an assumption, not something read out of the PSP contract. Leaves when someone checks the contract text: confirmed, this entry is discarded; wrong, the boundary moves and the comment in `_today()` is corrected.
